  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Migration at Work shows early scholarly uptake and strong reader interest: it has been cited 5 times and downloaded 2,746 times. The book also aligns with the SDG theme of reduced inequalities, suggesting clear relevance for policy and social research on migration, labour, and welfare.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Migration at Work has begun to circulate across the migration studies literature, with citations appearing steadily from 2021 through 2025. That pattern points to an emerging but still modest citation footprint, while the subject matter and the journal and book venues citing it indicate that the volume is being used in debates about migration and labour dynamics, integration, and related questions of mobility, governance, and inequality.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Usage data provide a stronger signal of reach than citations alone. The book has been downloaded 2,746 times through OAPEN, which suggests that it has attracted sustained reader attention since publication. In other words, the record shows that the volume is being actively consulted even as its citation base is still developing.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The thematic profile of the book helps explain that reach. Its focus on labour mobility, the structures shaping migration, and the imaginaries held by employers and regulating authorities connects it to civil society, sociology, political science, welfare, and social welfare, with a clear policy-facing relevance. The SDG alignment with reduced inequalities reinforces that the volume speaks to contemporary concerns about labour markets, migration governance, and social inclusion.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Funding support from KU Leuven, the Research Foundation Flanders (FWO), and Erasmus University Rotterdam situates the book within a substantial research environment. The record also shows open access availability in hybrid form, which likely helped widen access and use. Overall, the evidence points to a book with meaningful early scholarly and reader uptake, especially in migration-focused research communities, and with continuing potential for influence as the citation record matures.</p>",
